 "parts": [
  "Does the United States pay you at one hundred?",
  "No. Ireland does.",
  "The federal government has no hundredth-birthday payment that we could find.",
  "The closest thing is a White House greeting.",
  "But it is not automatic. Someone has to request it.",
  "In February twenty twenty-five, a viral chart suggested millions of people over one hundred were collecting Social Security.",
  "Fact-checkers found no evidence of that.",
  "Being in the database does not mean being paid.",
  "Now, Ireland.",
  "Since nineteen forty, Ireland has run a Centenarians' Bounty.",
  "Today it is a letter signed by the President, plus two thousand five hundred and forty euros.",
  "In America, you ask for a card.",
  "In Ireland, they send the money."
 ],
